00:26:31.210 --> 00:26:45.960
<v Ira Glass>And the reason I bring this up is a few weeks ago I was doing a show out here in Brooklyn. It was a very classy show with all these people, and a sold out show. So I put on a fancy suit. And I spent, like, six to eight hours on my hair.
<v Ira Glass>我提起这个的原因是几周前我在布鲁克林做一场演出。那是一场非常高级的演出，观众全是这类人，门票售罄。所以我穿了一套考究的西装。我还花了六到八个小时搞我的头发。

00:26:45.960 --> 00:26:53.450
<v Ira Glass>And the people putting the show on were like, oh, Dave, you've got to get out here on time. So I'm rushing to get out there. And I'm at 28th and Broadway. And the R train's right there.
<v Ira Glass>组织演出的人催我：“噢，戴夫，你得准时赶到那儿。”所以我急着出门。我在百老汇大道28街。R线地铁就在那儿。

00:26:53.450 --> 00:27:04.530
<v Ira Glass>So I'm like, oh, I'll take the R train. That's like a reputable train. And right before I'm going to go on the subway, I realize, oh, I'm so hungry. And then I look. And there's a gyro car right there.
<v Ira Glass>所以我心想：“噢，我会坐R线地铁。”那是趟靠谱的地铁。就在我准备进入地铁之前，我意识到：“噢，我太饿了。”然后我抬头一看。那儿正好有个希腊旋转烤肉车。

00:27:04.530 --> 00:27:14.920
<v Ira Glass>So I go to the gyro guy. I'm like, give my a gyro. And then he's got all the sauces, like the yogurt sauce, and the chili sauce, and the garlic sauce. And I'm just like, sauce the [BLEEP] out of that thing. And don't hold back on me.
<v Ira Glass>所以我走到那个人面前。我说：“给我来个肉卷。”他有各种酱汁，像酸奶酱、辣椒酱、蒜蓉酱。我就说：“把这东西给我狠狠地加酱。别跟我客气。”

00:27:14.920 --> 00:27:22.720
<v Ira Glass>And he just starts just hosing down the gyro. Like, calm down. And then finally, he gives me the gyro.
<v Ira Glass>于是他开始往肉卷上浇水似的加酱。我心想：“冷静点。”最后他把肉卷给了我。

00:27:22.720 --> 00:27:36.230
<v Ira Glass>And I go down into the subway. And the train comes right away. I get on it with the gyro. I start eating the gyro. And the sauces just start dripping all over my hands, and on the ground, and on my shoes and everything. And it's rush hour. And the train's, like, super crowded, and everything.
<v Ira Glass>我走进地铁站。车马上就来了。我带着肉卷上了车。我开始吃肉卷。酱汁开始滴得到处都是：滴在我的手上、地上、鞋子上，到处都是。正好赶上高峰期。地铁超级拥挤。

00:27:36.230 --> 00:27:48.090
<v Ira Glass>And I'm realizing, oh, I'm probably stinking up the whole car with this gyro. And people are probably looking at me thinking, that guy looks incredible. But it's not very cool what he's doing with that gyro.
<v Ira Glass>我意识到：“噢，我可能用这个肉卷把整个车厢弄得臭气熏天。”大家可能都在看着我想：“那个人看起来帅呆了，但他用肉卷搞出的动静不太酷。”

00:27:48.090 --> 00:28:01.340
<v Ira Glass>So I'm thinking the best thing that I can do for everyone on the train, and for the city of New York in general, is just get off the subway at the next stop, finish the gyro, get back on, go out to Brooklyn. And so I get off at the next stop, 23rd Street. Lightning quick decision.
<v Ira Glass>所以我心想，我能为列车上的人，也为纽约市所做的最好的事，就是在下一站下车，吃完肉卷，再上车去布鲁克林。于是我在下一站——23街——下了车。闪电般的决定。

00:28:01.340 --> 00:28:11.630
<v Ira Glass>And then I walk all the way to the end of the platform to eat my gyro. Because I don't even want to bother anyone on the platform with my gyro. I do cool [BLEEP] like this all the time.
<v Ira Glass>然后我一直走到站台尽头去吃我的肉卷。因为我甚至不想在站台上用我的肉卷打扰任何人。我总是做这种很酷的事。

00:28:11.630 --> 00:28:12.090
<v Ira Glass>[LAUGHTER]
<v Ira Glass>（笑声）

00:28:12.090 --> 00:28:28.670
<v Ira Glass>And so I go all the way down to the end of the platform. And you know how at the end of the subway they have the black metal storage bins? Not like a Norwegian black metal storage, which would be so cool. It's just like a regular black metal storage, almost like a dumpster or something.
<v Ira Glass>于是我走到站台最尽头。你们知道地铁尽头都有那种黑色金属储物箱吧？不是那种挪威黑金属那种（那是多酷啊），只是普通的黑色金属储物箱，几乎就像垃圾桶什么的。

00:28:28.670 --> 00:28:38.140
<v Ira Glass>So I'm stand next to it. And I've finished my gyro. And then I have the wrapper. And I'm looking around for a trash can to throw it out. And there's no trash can anywhere on the whole platform.
<v Ira Glass>我就站在它旁边。我吃完了肉卷。手里拿着包装纸。我环顾四周想找个垃圾桶扔掉它。但整个站台上压根就没有垃圾桶。

00:28:38.140 --> 00:28:42.640
<v Ira Glass>And it's too messy to put in my pocket. And I'm like, oh, I don't want to throw it on the ground. I don't want to throw it on the track.
